for title,tm,start,end,*_ in chapters:
 parts.append(f'\n### {title} | {tm}\n')
 for s in segments:
  if start <= float(s['start']) < end:parts.append(f"- {stamp(s['start'])}–{stamp(s['end'])}: {s['text'].strip()}\n")
parts.append('''\n## Source / release checklist\n- Locked source starting points: US State Department FRUS 1978 memo; American Alpine Club mission account; NASA/DOE RTG educational references; EPA/CDC plutonium risk references; actual Nanda Devi / Nanda Kot Commons works with per-file attribution/license validation. Recheck original pages and rights before editorial lock.\n- Pexels source should be a specific footage URL and actual subject; site license alone does not establish subject, people permissions for sensitive use, or historical authenticity.\n- Historical newspaper and Kohli archive permission requests are unsent; substitute accurate official source if no permission. A webpage capture is a webpage, not a scan of an original document.\n- Credits, data/source licenses, AI disclosures and final SRT ship alongside final, not after upload.\n\n## Deliverable status\nPlan only. No chapter is approved, no completed HD documentary exists, no exact line-by-line sync is verified, no rights clearance is implied. The verified previous working backup remains private on Kaggle.\n''')
